Connect material choices to the work that keeps them useful (@mat-life-evidence: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Economic-and-Environmental-Materials-Selection-MIT.lingua#r_36KMERFT8SDRP30MT63KQ5WS6C", #source "../sources/Sustainable-Materials-Selection-DOE.lingua#r_04ADQ1BN156GM7AVH5N2T7EAJZ", #source "../sources/Life-Cycle-Assessment-Detailed-Guide-ILCD.lingua#r_6YXH2DKX7XZRCE6XSCJ2QGJ3YX", #source "../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1", #source "../sources/Plastics-Recycling-Economy-NIST.lingua#r_4FMXC9V02YNV4DFSCCV0CVR8JN", #materials-engineering "../study/Three-studies-of-selection-service-and-recovery.lingua#r_6W6CEKY75RDY4YX46184KMTW7D") { r_0JRG7CM5616BS9TMYG9D5Q529G
**Read:** Finish [Economic and environmental issues in materials selection — MIT 3.080](../sources/Economic-and-Environmental-Materials-Selection-MIT.lingua#r_36KMERFT8SDRP30MT63KQ5WS6C), [Sustainable Materials Selection in Manufactured Products — DOE, 2023](../sources/Sustainable-Materials-Selection-DOE.lingua#r_04ADQ1BN156GM7AVH5N2T7EAJZ) and [Life-cycle assessment, detailed guidance — ILCD Handbook](../sources/Life-Cycle-Assessment-Detailed-Guide-ILCD.lingua#r_6YXH2DKX7XZRCE6XSCJ2QGJ3YX); use [Metal Recycling: Opportunities, Limits, Infrastructure — UNEP International Resource Panel](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1), [The U.S. Plastics Recycling Economy — Thomas, Kneifel and Butry](../sources/Plastics-Recycling-Economy-NIST.lingua#r_4FMXC9V02YNV4DFSCCV0CVR8JN) and the relevant full material-family references to close gaps in the chosen cases.

A material choice depends on a continuing system: feed identification, processing, utilities, tools, measurements, transport, inspection, repair and recovery. Each transfer can preserve or lose material quality and information. Record what another party needs to know about composition, history and uncertainty to use the output for its next function.

Connect proposed benefits to specific physical and organizational work. Reduced component mass may require more demanding processing; easier disassembly may alter service behavior; a durable material may need a difficult repair. The comparison should make those consequences inspectable rather than compressing them into a slogan.

**Work:** Trace one selected material from its source through at least two transfers and its next use after recovery. Identify the quantities, capabilities and information needed at each boundary. Close the functional, material and resource accounts, then state the unresolved evidence that most limits the proposed improvement.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Three studies of selection, service and recovery](../study/Three-studies-of-selection-service-and-recovery.lingua#r_6W6CEKY75RDY4YX46184KMTW7D).

